# To-do-list skill routing

When the request matches a phase below, read and follow the matching project skill under `.cursor/skills/` before freestyling.

| Intent | Skill |
|--------|-------|
| Which skill / workflow / what’s next | `todo-workflow` |
| MVP scope, brainstorm, cut features | `todo-office-hours` |
| Specs, tickets, backlog split | `todo-spec` |
| Architecture, data model lock | `todo-plan-eng-review` |
| Design system / DESIGN.md | `todo-design-consultation` |
| Plan UI slop check | `todo-plan-design-review` |
| Design variants | `todo-design-shotgun` |
| Lock HTML/CSS from approved design | `todo-design-html` |
| Implemented UI polish | `todo-design-review` |
| AI-slop / 밤티 redesign (Hallmark) | `todo-hallmark` |
| Apple HIG / a11y craft review | `todo-apple-design` |
| Multi-skill UI/UX orchestration | `todo-uiux` |
| QA report without fixes | `todo-qa-only` |
| Bugs / root cause | `todo-investigate` |
| Architecture/data-flow diagram | `todo-diagram` |

Always load `.cursor/skills/todo-workflow/constraints.md` and `excel-domain.md` for product work.

Design anti-slop pack sources: `.cursor/skills/DESIGN-SKILLS.md`.

Do not start deploy, ship, land-and-deploy, or canary work unless the user explicitly overrides later.
